    <div id="statement">
        <p id="description">
            I'm a PhD student in 3D vision and robotics at the
            <a href="https://www.caor.minesparis.psl.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> Centre de Robotique, Mines Paris – PSL</a>,
            working on 3D perception and representation learning for autonomous robotics
            in natural and unstructured environments. I'm particularly interested in cross-modal and
            self-supervised learning for robust 3D perception. My PhD is conducted
            in collaboration with the <a href="http://u2is.ensta-paris.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> U2IS lab of ENSTA Paris.</a>

            <br><br>

            Previously, I conducted research on foundation model-based perturbation
            modeling on spatial proteomics data at
            <a href="https://aimm.epfl.ch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> EPFL's AIMM lab</a>.
            I graduated as a research engineer from ENSTA Paris and studied
            machine learning and computer vision in the MVA (Mathematics, Vision,
            Learning) master's programme at ENS Paris-Saclay.
        </p>

        <p>github: <a href="https://github.com/amine-maazizi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@amine-maazizi</a></p>
        <p>email: <a href="#" class="email" aria-label="Copy Mines Paris email address">amine (dot) maazizi [at] minesparis (dot) psl (dot) eu</a></p>
